    "link": "https://x.com/ChennaiRains/status/2101483121443233979?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet",
    "snippet": "Two events yesterday, IMD announced the start of monsoon withdrawal from NW India and also announced the formation of LPA over North Andaman Sea. The LPA is expected to intensify into a Deep Depression over the next couple of days and reach AP / Odisha coast around Wednesday. Meanwhile convergence influenced by the LPA will bring another widespread thunderstorms over Peninsular India. Once again parts of Krishnagiri, Dharmapuri, Tirupathur, Kallakurichi, Tiruvannamalai, Cuddalore, Villupuram, Perambalur and Ariyalur dts may be hotspots. In yesterday's post I mentioned Chennai may see widespread thundestorms one day between yesterday and tomorrrow. This period also represents the best chance for Chennai and I still believe we may see thunderstorms either today or tomorrow even though yesterday was a disappointment.",
